---
id: air-fried-chicken-breast
title: Baked Chicken Breast
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 330

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Trim any excess fat or tenderloin tendon from @boneless-chicken-breast{1%package}. Pat thoroughly dry on all sides using paper towels to remove surface purge so the seasoning adheres evenly.

Rub the @boneless-chicken-breast evenly with @olive-oil{1%tsp}, then coat all sides with @kosher-salt{1/2%tsp}, @black-pepper{1/4%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1/2%tsp}, and @smoked-paprika{1/2%tsp}.

Set the #oven to convection 200°C (400°F) and let it preheat fully, about 10 to 15 minutes. Arrange the breasts on the mesh basket of the #crisper-tray with space between them, so the circulating air reaches every side, juices drip away, and no flipping is needed. Bake on the middle rack for ~bake-time{17%min}, checking from the 15-minute mark, until the internal temperature reaches 71°C to 74°C (160°F–165°F) at the thickest part checked with a #meat-thermometer.

Let the chicken rest undisturbed for ~rest-time{5%min} so carryover heat completes cooking and juices redistribute into the meat fibers. Distribute whole breasts (or slice into thick medallions, ~165 g each) into 2 separate meal prep containers, drizzling any rested juices from the board over the portions.
